P1.9: correlator catch-all + numeric port sort; docker-down is a failure

Three correctness bugs:

1. Correlator silently dropped any asset whose category no pass handles, quietly
   breaking the module's stated "nothing is dropped" invariant. Added a catch-all
   pass (9b) that routes unhandled categories to their project bucket (else System)
   as `other_assets` + a warning log, and an `other_assets` field on every app.

2. listening_ports were sorted with key=str (lexicographic): 100 sorted before 22.
   Removed them from the string-keyed sort and sort numerically (ints only).

3. Docker-daemon-down was reported as a SUCCESSFUL scan. The scanner called
   add_error -> status "partial_success"; the scan job only treated "failed" as a
   failure, so a totally-down daemon (zero docker assets) reported success AND the
   correlator then rebuilt from zero, wiping the whole docker inventory. Now:
   - DockerScanner.scan() raises when the daemon is unreachable -> status "failed".
   - the scan job distinguishes failed vs degraded (partial per-item errors),
     records degraded_scanners, and sets the run status to
     failed | degraded | success. Scans.jsx renders a degraded (amber) pill.

